# config.example/outpost.env - the shared, per-host facts.
#
# Read FIRST, by every service, before its own compose.env, because `just` feeds docker
# compose this file and the per-service compose.env together, and the later file only
# overrides a key the earlier one also sets. Put the value every host repeats ONCE here,
# and keep a service's compose.env to what that service alone needs: this is the rule that
# stops the same address being written once per service and rotting in N places.
#
# Every value below is a placeholder. Addresses are RFC 5737 (192.0.2.0/24) and RFC 6598
# (100.64.0.0/10) documentation space. This file is gitignored, so it never leaves the
# estate; a fresh clone gets it from config.example/ by running `just init` and then edits
# it here.
#
# Each host has its own copy of this file (one per host). On a two-host estate the proxy
# host and the app host each carry their own OUTPOST_CONFIG_DIR/outpost.env with their own
# addresses.

# The three values that every service's compose file interpolates are the "shared per-host
# facts" and live here, one place each, rather than being repeated in every service dir.
# A service that needs only these interpolates them from this file and lists nothing extra.
#
# Per-service facts that one service consumes live in that service's own file, by R1's
# "one value, one place". The ACME email and domain are Caddy facts (00_proxy/app.env),
# because that is where they are read.

# This host's single LAN address, e.g. from `ip -4 addr show eth0`.
# 192.0.2.10 is RFC 5737 documentation space. Replace it with this host's LAN address.
# Never 0.0.0.0: that would bind every published service to every interface and reopen the
# ingress that the per-host nftables rulesets exist to close.
BIND_ADDR=192.0.2.10

# This host's tailnet address, from `tailscale ip -4`.
# 100.64.0.0/10 is the Tailscale CGNAT range (RFC 6598); the whole tailnet is one range,
# so no estate-specific value belongs here except the host's own address in it.
TAILSCALE_ADDR=100.64.0.10

# This host's data root. Caddy's data and config live under it (see 00_proxy).
# The other services declare their own data roots in their compose.env; do not centralise
# them, because a data root chosen for one service is not necessarily right for another.
APPDATA=/srv/outpost
